{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>There shall step a star out of Jacob</b> – Because the Messiah will gather the dispersed of Israel from the end of the earth, he likens him to a star that courses through the firmament from the end of the heavens, as is said of him: \"and behold, with the clouds of heaven one like a son of man\" etc. (Daniel 7:13). And he says that he sees to a distant time, that a star will step from the end of the heavens, and there shall arise from him a ruling tribe <b>and it shall smite the corners of Moab, and tear down all the children of Seth</b> – the son of Adam, who is the father of all the nations. And he mentioned \"the corners of Moab\" to inform Balak that his people will not fall into the hand of Israel now, but in the end of days Moab will not be saved from the hand of the ruling tribe that is in him. And the sense of \"the corners of Moab\" is to say that this tribe will tear down all the children of Seth, and Moab will not be saved from his hand even though they are shorn at the corners and have no name among the nations, nor will they do battle with Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:26.985705791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}